From 3ed345b017c90290cddf5e8996eafae6aa858689 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Radu Constantinescu <rdu@amazon.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 15:41:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fs, internal/http: add custom HTTP request headers via
 snapshot labels

A snapshot label containerd.io/snapshot/remote/soci.header.<name> = <value>
adds the header <name>: <value> to the registry requests the snapshotter
makes. Callers can use this to identify or correlate their requests.

source.HeadersFromLabels reads the labels. fs.fs puts the headers on the
context at each mount entry point (Mount, MountParallel, MountLocal), in the
neighboring-layer pre-resolution loop, and in preloadAllLayers. Each
httpFetcher captures them once at creation and re-attaches them on fetch,
check, and refreshURL. AuthClient.Do sets them on the outgoing request, so
layer, index, and zTOC fetches all carry them.

Names and values are validated with golang.org/x/net/http/httpguts. The value
check rejects CR and LF, so a label cannot inject a second header or split the
request. Reserved headers set by the snapshotter or a shared library (Range,
Accept-Encoding, Accept, Content-Type, Content-Length, Authorization,
User-Agent, Referer) are dropped with a WARN at both the parser and the sink.
An invalid or reserved label never fails the mount.

Signed-off-by: Radu Constantinescu <rdu@amazon.com>
